cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ETDL in your work, please cite the specification."
title: "ETDL Specification — Event Tree Definition Language"
abstract: >-
  A declarative, design-time domain-specific language (DSL) for reliability-aware,
  event-driven business processes. Models causal sequences as event trees
  (IEC 62502:2010) and failure probability as fault trees (IEC 61025:2006),
  resolved against AsyncAPI 3.0 contracts, and compiles to service code.
authors:
  - family-names: "ETDL Contributors"
    given-names: ""
    website: "https://github.com/usamassem"
keywords:
  - event tree analysis
  - fault tree analysis
  - IEC 61025
  - IEC 62502
  - reliability engineering
  - probabilistic risk assessment
  - event-driven architecture
  - microservices
  - domain-specific language
  - AsyncAPI
  - code generation
license: CC-BY-4.0
# Note: the specification is under development and NOT yet released;
# a formal citation should not imply a released, stable version.
url: "https://github.com/usamassem/etdl-specification"
